==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|raja}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|hi|राजा}} and {{bor|en|ur|راجا|tr=rājā}}, from {{der|en|sa|राजन्||king, prince}}, from {{der|en|inc-pro|*Hrā́ȷ́ā||king}}, from {{der|en|iir-pro|*Hrā́ȷ́ā}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵ-ō}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵs|t=ruler, king}}. {{doublet|en|Rex|rex|roy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɑː.dʒə/|/ˈɹɑː.ʒə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a [[Hindu]] [[prince]] or [[ruler]] in [[India]].
# Any of various [[nymphalid]] butterflies of the [[genus]] {{taxlink|Charaxes|genus|ver=190708}}.

