Borrowed from {{bor|ceb|hi|राजा}}, from {{der|ceb|sa|राजन्||king, prince}}, from {{der|ceb|inc-pro|*Hrā́ȷ́ā||king}}, from {{der|ceb|iir-pro|*Hrā́ȷ́ā}}, from {{der|ceb|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵ-ō}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵs|t=ruler, king}}. {{doublet|ceb|rey}} and its [[Reyes#ceb|derived surnames]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|General Cebuano}} {{IPA|ceb|/ˈrad͡ʒɐ/}}

Notes: Also sometimes pronounced as /ˈrahɐ/, inspired by [[w:Spanish_orthrography|Spanish orthography]].

===Noun===
{{head|ceb|noun}}

# {{lb|ceb|historical}} The ruler of the Indianized [[rajahnate]] polities of the Philippines. A notable example is the [[w:Rajahnate_of_Cebu|Rajahnate of Cebu]].

